    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40526" root="نكر" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَكِرَةٌ</span></b>  <i>Ignorance,</i> &amp;c., (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنْكَار</span>,) of a thing; (TA;)
<i>contr. of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعْرِفَةٌ</span>; (S, K;) and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَكَارَةٌ</span></b> ; syn.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَهَالَةٌ</span>; as in the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِيهِ نَكَارَةٌ</span> [<i>In him is ignorance</i>]. (A.) See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَكَرَةٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [As <i>contr. of</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعْرِفَةٌ</span>, it is also, in grammar, an epithet applied
to a noun, signifying <i>Indeterminate,</i> or <i>indefinite.</i>]

  </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
